-- title:
--   Poincaré bundle along the Abel–Jacobi image of a ℚ̄-point
-- statement:
--   The setting is the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring, together with a designated relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ and its Poincaré bundle.
--
--   *Arithmetic data.* A prime $p$, a non-zero natural number $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and an element $\zeta \in L$ that is a primitive $p$-th root of unity. The field $K$ is an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, and `hK` requires $K =$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Further, $A$ is a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAp`) and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), and $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \subseteq L \subseteq K$. The element $j \in K$ is non-zero and satisfies `hj`: its image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ is the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the $q$-expansion of the modular function $j$. Finally $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` is an $A$-algebra and an $L$-algebra, compatibly.
--
--   *The model and its Jacobian.* Write $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ for [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252), assumed proper. The datum $\varepsilon$ is a section of $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, and $D$ is a `RelativePic0Designation`: a scheme $D.P$ with a structure morphism `D.toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and a zero section. The hypothesis `hrep` asserts that $D$ represents, with respect to $\varepsilon$, the subfunctor of rigidified line bundles cut out by `algEquivZeroCut` (fibrewise algebraic equivalence to zero); its chosen witness `hrep.some` supplies the Poincaré bundle `hrep.some.poincare`, a rigidified line bundle on $X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} D.P$, universal for that condition. The hypotheses `hsm` and `hsep` require `D.toBase` to be smooth and separated.
--
--   *Base change to $L$.* `hsmL` and `hgiL` require the base change $X_L \to \operatorname{Spec} L$ to be smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral; `hprL` and `hgcL` require `pullback.snd D.toBase (specMap A L)`, the base change of `D.toBase` to $L$, to be proper and geometrically connected. The hypothesis `hDL` is the corresponding representability statement over $L$: the base change `D.baseChange L` represents the `algEquivZeroCut` condition for $X_L$ with the base-changed section `sectionBaseChange L ε`, with Poincaré bundle `hDL.poincare`. The morphism `ajL` is a morphism $X_L \to (D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,L).\mathrm{toBase}$ over $\operatorname{Spec} L$ (the Abel–Jacobi morphism over $L$), `hajLε` says that it sends the base-changed section to the zero section of `D.baseChange L`, and `hajL` is its defining property: for every field $K'$, every morphism $t : \operatorname{Spec} K' \to \operatorname{Spec} L$ and every $t$-point $x$ of $X_L$, the pullback of `hDL.poincare` along $x \cdot \mathrm{ajL}$ has underlying module isomorphic to the line bundle of the relative effective Cartier divisor `RelEffCartierDiv.ofPoint` of $x$ tensored with the ideal module of `RelEffCartierDiv.ofPoint` of $t$ followed by the base-changed section. The hypothesis `hPL` ties the two Poincaré bundles: `hDL.poincare.L` is isomorphic to the module obtained by `BaseChange.ofR` from the pullback of `hrep.some.poincare` along the first projection of `pullback D.toBase (specMap A L)`.
--
--   *The $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-fibre.* $M_\eta$ is a `CurveModel` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182), and $e_\eta$ is an isomorphism from $M_\eta.C$ to `pullback X (specMap A (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` compatible with the structure morphisms (`heη`). The instance `Mη_chart_nonempty` asserts that the preimage under $e_\eta$ followed by the first projection of the image of the finite chart [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.ιFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L231) is non-empty, and `hMηpin` pins the identification down: for every element $a$ of the finite chart algebra `chartAlgFin A K j`, its germ at the generic point, transported through `Mη.ffEquiv.symm` into `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` and viewed as a Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, equals the coefficientwise image along $L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of $a$ read as a Laurent series over $L$. The hypothesis `hgal` is Galois equivariance: for every $g \in \mathrm{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ fixing the image of $L$ pointwise and all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, x'$ of $M_\eta.C$, if $x'$ followed by $e_\eta$ and the first projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}(g)$ followed by the same composite for $x$, then `Mη.pointEquivPlace x'` is the translate of `Mη.pointEquivPlace x` by the semilinear automorphism [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (x1FunctionField (M * p)) g`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54).
--
--   *Hecke, diamond and Galois bookkeeping.* `hin` is [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondInputsAll (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L58) and `hcomm` is [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondCommuteBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L54) (commutation of the Hecke and diamond generators at level $Mp$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$). The group $L \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}} L$ acts on $A$ by semiring automorphisms, compatibly with $A \to L$ (`hΓA`). The equivalence `gpts` identifies [`ModularCurve.JOne (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L186), the degree-zero divisor class group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with the set of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of `D.toBase`.
--
--   *Abel–Jacobi over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.* The morphism $\overline{\mathrm{aj}} : M_\eta.C \to D.P$ and the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $\bar\varepsilon$ of $M_\eta.C$ satisfy: `hajbar`, $\overline{\mathrm{aj}} = e_\eta$ followed by $k_L$, by `ajL`, and by the first projection of `pullback D.toBase (specMap A L)`, where $k_L$ is a morphism from `pullback X (specMap A (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` to `pullback X (specMap A L)` compatible with both projections (`hkL₁`, `hkL₂`); `hajbar_over`, that $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$ lies over $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$; `hεbar`, that $\bar\varepsilon$ induces the base change of $\varepsilon$; `hεbar_aj`, that $\bar\varepsilon$ followed by $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$ is the base change of the zero section of $D$; and `hpts_aj`, that for all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, s$ of $M_\eta.C$ with $s$ inducing the base change of $\varepsilon$ there is a degree-zero divisor $D_v$ on `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` equal to $[\,\mathrm{place}(x)\,] - [\,\mathrm{place}(s)\,]$, with $\mathrm{place} =$ `Mη.pointEquivPlace`, whose class under `gpts` is the point $x$ followed by $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$.
--
--   *Conclusion.* Let $y$ be a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $M_\eta.C$, let $\bar y$ be the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $X$ given by $y$ followed by $e_\eta$ and the first projection (`hybar`), and let $a$ be the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of `D.toBase` given by $y$ followed by $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$ (`ha`). Then the underlying module of the pullback of the Poincaré bundle `hrep.some.poincare` along $a$ is isomorphic, as a module on `pullback X (specMap A (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`, to the tensor product of the line bundle of `RelEffCartierDiv.ofPoint` at $\bar y$ — the dual of the kernel ideal sheaf of the graph of $\bar y$ — with the ideal module of `RelEffCartierDiv.ofPoint` at the base change of $\varepsilon$, namely that kernel ideal sheaf itself. Equivalently, $\mathcal{P}|_a \cong \mathcal{O}(\bar y) \otimes \mathcal{O}(\varepsilon_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}})^{-1}$. The assertion is the existence of such an isomorphism, no particular isomorphism being named.
--
--   This is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-fibre normalisation of the Abel–Jacobi morphism for the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$: it records that restricting the Poincaré bundle along the Abel–Jacobi image of a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $\bar y$ returns the point bundle of $\bar y$ twisted by the inverse of the bundle of the base section, transporting the corresponding statement over $L$ through the pinned model $M_\eta$. It is the common input to the geometric realisations of the diamond operators and of the Galois action on the Jacobian model, being cited by [`ModularCurve.XOneP.pts_diamondGen_smul_eq_comp_transport_of_abelJacobi_of_diamondModelAut_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.pts_diamondGen_smul_eq_comp_transport_of_abelJacobi_of_diamondModelAut_twoChartModel_x1_mul) and [`ModularCurve.XOneP.pts_smul_eq_specMap_comp_comp_of_galoisModelAut_of_classifies_abelJacobi_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.pts_smul_eq_specMap_comp_comp_of_galoisModelAut_of_classifies_abelJacobi_twoChartModel_x1_mul).
